<section id="about" class="pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-8 md:pb-12 bg-mint/25">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-ink mb-8">About Manaaki Midwives</h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-ink/80 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Manaaki Midwives is a close group of Lead Maternity Carer (LMC) midwives based in Hutt Central,
          supporting whānau across Upper and Lower Hutt and Wainuiomata.
        </p>
        <p>
          <em>Manaaki</em>, to care for, support and uplift, is at the heart of how we work.
          We believe pregnancy and birth are normal life events that deserve respect, and we walk
          alongside you with clear information and steady support so you can make the choices that
          are right for you and your pēpi.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Shared care -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-10 shadow-sm border border-mint/50">
      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl md:text-3xl text-ink mb-6 text-center">Our approach to shared care</h3>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Each of our midwives shares equal responsibility for your care, and together we provide
          evidence-based care tailored to you throughout pregnancy and birth.
        </p>
        <p>
          We understand that continuity of care is important, and that seeing a familiar face throughout
          your journey matters. That's why our shared-care model gives you the chance to get to know all
          four of our midwives during your pregnancy.
        </p>
        <p>
          While shared care means you will be cared for by more than one midwife, it also means you have
          a whole team who knows you, communicates closely and shares responsibility for your care.
        </p>
        <p>
          From your booking appointment through pregnancy and birth, our team will support you every step
          of the way. Whether you are planning a hospital birth, a home birth or a planned caesarean, we aim
          to provide care that respects your individual needs and choices.
        </p>
        <p>
          After your birth, our team will continue to care for you for the first 72 hours, allowing time for
          postnatal assessments, support and a birth debrief. We will then provide a comprehensive handover to
          our dedicated postnatal midwife, who will continue supporting you and your pēpi through the rest of
          the postnatal period.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
